# Accepted residuals. One entry: an accepted residual has to be a finding with
# nothing to fix, and only this one still is.
#
# Every ID here is ignored in every image and in the fs scan: trivy's plain
# ignore file cannot scope an ID to one image.
#
# Deleted, not re-dated: 4 mini-baas-waf IDs and 26 mini-baas-vault IDs, checked
# on 2026-09-23 with trivy 0.74.0 and the gate's flags (--severity HIGH,CRITICAL
# --ignore-unfixed).
# - waf (CVE-2026-5773, -6276, -7598, -6732): in no package of
#   ghcr.io/univers42/grobase-waf:latest (Debian 13.7), at any severity.
# - vault: infra/docker/services/vault/Dockerfile's FROM hashicorp/vault:1.21
#   resolves to 1.21.4 (Go 1.25.7), the last 1.21 tag. There, 16 of the IDs are
#   fixable HIGH/CRITICAL, 6 are HIGH with no fix, 3 are MEDIUM (the gate drops
#   those 9) and 1 is absent. Vault 2.1.1 carries none of the 26. They stay out
#   because 12 of them are also in grobase-gotrue and 10 in grobase-loki and
#   grobase-mc, where the vault reason does not hold, and because the vault image
#   fails the gate without them: 30 other fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings that no
#   entry here ever covered. The fix is the base bump to Vault 2.x, which ships to
#   deployments and needs a human trigger.
#
# GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8 (RUSTSEC-2026-0104): rustls-webpki 0.101.7 in
# src/data-plane-router/Cargo.lock -- the one scanned lockfile holding 0.101.x
# (realtime-agnostic/Cargo.lock is 0.103.13; vendor/ is skip-dirs). Two paths,
# both over rustls 0.21.12: tiberius 0.12.3 -> tokio-rustls 0.24.1 (mssql, always
# built) and aws-smithy-http-client 1.1.13 -> hyper-rustls 0.24.2 (dynamodb,
# opt-in). The bug is a panic parsing a CRL, and the advisory scopes it to callers
# that pass RevocationOptions; both paths build rustls-0.21 CLIENT configs
# with_no_client_auth() and load no CRL, so it is unreachable here. Drop this when
# tiberius leaves rustls 0.21. REVIEW-BY 2026-12-23, enforced by the exp: below.
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8 exp:2026-12-23
